WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.780
Going to college in 1940 was not easy, financially.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.960
I have an aunt who lived in Baton Rouge, my mother’s sister who lived in Baton Rouge,

3
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.300
and I lived with her during the time that I was a student at LSU.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:23.020
She was superintendent of nurses at the Baton Rouge General Hospital and we lived on Government Street,

5
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.300
not far from the hospital, which was on Government Street then.

6
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.420
And we would walk down to Ferdinand Street and catch a ride.

7
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.160
People would pass by on the way to the university and hold up two fingers or three fingers,

8
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.640
[meaning] they could take two people or three people,

9
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:46.120
and we always hoped somebody would come along and pick us up and we didn’t have to use the money for the bus.
